Sound: an exponential release / decrease reaches ENVX 0 (arithmetic shift as PCSX2 and DuckStation); keyed-off voices no longer stay taken and fill the effects core in combat. GOW_SND_VOICESTATS=1 prints voices in use / in release every 5 s.

diff --git a/PS2Recomp/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/core/sound_engine.cpp b/PS2Recomp/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/core/sound_engine.cpp
--- a/PS2Recomp/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/core/sound_engine.cpp
+++ b/PS2Recomp/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/core/sound_engine.cpp
@@ -497,8 +497,12 @@
         step <<= std::max(0, 11 - shiftValue);
         if (exponential && increase && v.envelope > 0x6000)
             cycles *= 4u;
+        // gow-native-pc: an arithmetic shift, as PCSX2 and DuckStation (psx-spx: Step * Level / 8000h on the hardware's
+        // two's complement value). A division truncates toward zero: the step became 0 near silence and an exponential
+        // release / decrease stopped above 0 (at 1/8 of full level with slow rates), the voice kept sounding and stayed taken:
+        // in combat the effects core filled its 24 voices with them and new hits found none free.
         if (exponential && !increase)
-            step = step * v.envelope / 0x8000;
+            step = (step * v.envelope) >> 15;
 
         if (++v.envelopeCounter >= cycles)
         {
